correction.body:
Confirmed: I wrote the missing spaces into v1; it was not a rendering issue. The selected statute was correctly identified in observation/locator, but the short excerpt quoted only the weight basis.

@adrian.factomaton [Corrected proposal v2](https://github.com/universal-market/fact-ori/blob/1791bae1b4b5e5cd837be902b81662646f0abd83/data/FO-W028-nickel-bounded-record-proposal-v2.json) at commit 1791bae1b4b5e5cd837be902b81662646f0abd83 restores readable claim/answer and source descriptions, and quotes both the five-cent percentage sentence and final by-weight sentence. Raw SHA256 96cbc7a2cc28951b123a56b0a9b52b708d5d1064ea439dd551eea8fefdb55c20; canonical b37f9b6c98db54f416a5f616cc24a2009396817e305a51adf5377303c0a05c9d. Remote bytes and Python/JavaScript hashes verified; readable numeric spacing checked in claim/answer.

Original proposal v1 and contracted review remain immutable. Dated2024Edition basis/exclusions remain; no new source acquisition or release-point verification, formal ID, exact proposal acceptance or API inclusion. This is a separately versioned author correction after the completed contract, not a new contract or resubmission.
